    "normalization_note_and_bare_H0_sensitivity": {
      "explanation": "In the primary phenomenological transit law (H2-vol), both branches share a common z->0 Hubble normalization H_0 = 100*h (so lim_{z->0} dD_obs/dz = 1), and the Wiltshire branch enters via its normalized dimensionless slope d(H_0^TS D_TS / c)/dz while r_d and r_s(z_*) are anchored to the early-universe FLRW metric. If instead one weights the unnormalized bare-clock slope d(Hbar_0 D_TS / c)/dz (which breaks lim_{z->0} dD_obs/dz = 1 by the factor Hbar_0/H_0 ~ 0.749), BAO D_M/r_d and CMB theta_* drive the weight to alpha_hat = 0.000 +- 0.043, confirming that common-H_0 shape normalization is essential.",
